  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="4f89-c0ad-90a9-572b" name="Palmyran (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #48 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). Palmyra was a Roman client state in the Middle East, which gained a brief period of independence and became a threat to Rome before being defeated. When the Eastern Emperor Valerian was captured by the Sassanids, the Palmyran King Odenathus was appointed commander of the Eastern Roman forces. His success in defeating the Sassanids led him to rebel. After his assassination his wife Zenobia continued to lead Palmyran armies, overrunning Asia Minor and Egypt before being defeated by Aurelian. This army can therefore be modelled as a variant on the Eastern Roman army, or as the independent forces of the insurrection. 

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Palmyran]
  Cavalry: at least 50%
  Characters: up to 20%
  Infantry: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 20% Cavalry: At least 50% Infantry: Up to 25% Artillery: Up to one engine per 1200 points Allies: Up to 50%: Middle Imperial Roman</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
